      "index": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 782452988,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1763070235,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why JWT?\n→ Stateless auth; server validates a signed token on each request.\n\nWhy BCrypt?\n→ Store a slow salted hash instead of the password.\n\nWhy localStorage?\n→ Simple demo persistence across refreshes; XSS risk in production.\n\nWhy CORS?\n→ Browser sees React :3000 and Spring :8080 as different origins.\n\nWhy disable CSRF?\n→ We are not using automatically-sent session cookies for authentication.\n\nWhat if JWT is edited?\n→ Signature validation fails → request remains anonymous → 401.\n\nWhat would production add?\n→ Refresh tokens, roles/authorities, rate limiting, real DB, managed secret/vault.",
      "fontSize": 19,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 15,
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why JWT?\n→ Stateless auth; server validates a signed token on each request.\n\nWhy BCrypt?\n→ Store a slow salted hash instead of the password.\n\nWhy localStorage?\n→ Simple demo persistence across refreshes; XSS risk in production.\n\nWhy CORS?\n→ Browser sees React :3000 and Spring :8080 as different origins.\n\nWhy disable CSRF?\n→ We are not using automatically-sent session cookies for authentication.\n\nWhat if JWT is edited?\n→ Signature validation fails → request remains anonymous → 401.\n\nWhat would production add?\n→ Refresh tokens, roles/authorities, rate limiting, real DB, managed secret/vault.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
